## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience building production ML pipelines in AWS with strict data locality, latency targets, and privacy. Assesses ability to combine PrivateLink, Lake Formation, Feature Store, canary deployment, drift monitoring, and cost governance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker PrivateLink
- Lake Formation data access
- Feature Store
- Endpoint traffic splitting (canary)
- Drift detection & retraining triggers
- DP privacy controls and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example drift score calculation (KS statistic placeholder)
function ksDrift(p, q) {
  let max = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < p.length; i++) {
    max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(p[i] - q[i]));
  }
  return max;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rollback if canary drift triggers fire?
- What metrics and thresholds would you alert on for latency, FP rate, and drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates ability to design private, language-aware ML inference at scale with strict data locality and per-tenant isolation. Tests routing logic, canary deployment strategies, and cross-language drift handling.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker multi-model vs. per-language endpoints
- PrivateLink data residency and IAM isolation
- Canary rollouts and per-language versioning
- Model Registry + Pipelines for safe promotions
- Tenant-scoped storage and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Language route resolver
function routeEndpoint(lang) {
  const map = {
    en: 'ep-en',
    fr: 'ep-fr',
    de: 'ep-de'
  };
  return map[lang] || 'ep-default';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates multi-tenant isolation, model versioning, and controlled rollout in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker endpoint variants and traffic shifting
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines for versioning
- Tenant-level routing and isolation, least-privilege IAM, PrivateLink
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify and per-tenant monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for per-tenant routing in the inference container
function route(event){
  const tenant = event.tenant_id;
  const variant = tenantVariantMap[tenant] || 'prod';
  // forward to the corresponding variant
  return invokeVariant(variant, event.payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback safety across tenants during a failed canary?
- How would you model per-tenant cost and scale limits in DynamoDB and CloudWatch?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses design for multi-tenant ML services with strict data residency, private networking, and production-grade reliability, including canarying, drift handling, and cost accounting.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Multi-tenant routing architectures (per-tenant vs shared endpoint)
- Canary deployments with automatic rollback on drift/latency
- SageMaker Model Monitor for drift and quality checks
- KMS encryption and data residency controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing logic (illustrative only)
function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const endpoint = selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId);
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, payload);
}

function selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId) {
  // tenants mapped to endpoints or routing keys
  const map = {
    't1': 'endpoint-arn-1',
    't2': 'endpoint-arn-2'
  };
  return map[tenantId] || 'shared-endpoint-arn';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design per-tenant quotas and rate limiting to prevent tail latency spikes?
- What metrics and alerting would you configure to detect drift early and trigger rollback?
